# Dynamic element conversion to a type keeps the stored subtype

Verifies a type-only conversion changes the representation while preserving the
element's own subtype, so a `2cm` element becomes `2cm` in the requested type
rather than losing its unit.

>>> source
let sizes: int[] = [2cm]
let index = 0
print(sizes[index] -> to(decimal))

<<< stdout
2cm

<<< stderr
